monitor: skip expired mirror weakptrs in onDisconnect

CMonitor::m_mirrors is a std::vector<PHLMONITORREF> — weak references — and can
hold entries whose monitor is already gone. When the mirrored output itself
disconnects, onDisconnect() walks that list and calls m->setMirror("") on each
entry unconditionally, so an expired one calls setMirror with this == nullptr:

    setMirror+0x145: mov 0x538(%r12),%rdx   ; r12 (this) == 0, reading m_mirrorOf

Backtrace is always setMirror() <- onDisconnect() <- onConnect()::lambda#6 <-
Aquamarine::SDRMConnector::disconnect(). Reproduces by powering off the source
monitor of a `mirror` rule (DP monitors drop off DRM on power-off).

setMirror("") also erases the caller's entry from the very m_mirrors being
iterated, so iterate a copy as well.

Applies to Hyprland 8b7aefe32e3459a6e3a92cbd6dd6c638d1b8dbdd (v0.56.0).

--- a/src/output/Monitor.cpp
+++ b/src/output/Monitor.cpp
@@ -418,8 +418,12 @@
     }
 
     if (!m_mirrors.empty()) {
-        for (auto const& m : m_mirrors) {
-            m->setMirror("");
+        // m_mirrors holds weak refs that may already be expired, and setMirror("")
+        // erases from m_mirrors, so iterate a copy and skip dead entries.
+        const auto mirrors = m_mirrors;
+        for (auto const& m : mirrors) {
+            if (auto mon = m.lock())
+                mon->setMirror("");
         }
 
         Config::monitorRuleMgr()->scheduleReload();
